# {{ .Name }} ({{ .Type }})

The `portainer_endpoint_snapshot` action takes a snapshot of one environment (endpoint), or of every environment when `endpoint_id` is unset, so Portainer's view of containers, stacks and resources is current.

> **Requirements:** Terraform >= 1.14 (actions). OpenTofu does not support actions; there, and with older Terraform, use the [`portainer_endpoint_snapshot` resource](../resources/endpoint_snapshot.md), which runs the same operation when it is created.

## Example Usage

### Run it from a lifecycle `action_trigger`

```hcl
action "portainer_endpoint_snapshot" "all" {}

# Refresh Portainer's view of every environment after a stack is deployed.
resource "portainer_stack" "app" {
  # ...

  lifecycle {
    action_trigger {
      events  = [after_create, after_update]
      actions = [action.portainer_endpoint_snapshot.all]
    }
  }
}
```

### Run it on demand

```shell
terraform apply -invoke action.portainer_endpoint_snapshot.all
```

## Lifecycle & Behavior

- The action runs only when it is invoked: from an `action_trigger` on the events listed there, or with `terraform apply -invoke`. A plan lists the invocations it would run; nothing is stored in state, so there is nothing to destroy and no `triggers` argument is needed to run it again.
- It sends the same requests as the `portainer_endpoint_snapshot` resource does when it is created, with the same defaults, and fails the apply with the same errors.

{{ .SchemaMarkdown | trimspace }}

## Attributes Reference

Actions have no attributes: nothing they return can be referenced elsewhere in the configuration.
